\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Thresholds on the standard deviation $\sigma _\theta $ of an elevation estimate as a function of its mean $\bar  {\theta }$, for the Ping360 ($b = 25^\circ $) and $k = 3$, computed from Eqs.~\eqref  {eq:msis_sigmal}--\eqref  {eq:msis_sigmaT}. Estimates below $\sigma _T = \min (\sigma _l, \sigma _m)$ (shaded) keep their beta distribution; the others are replaced by the uniform distribution. Fig.~9 of \citet  {breux2020elevation} shows the same thresholds, as variances, for a $35^\circ $ beam.}}{17}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
